# ADR-054: Admin SA-Authorized Offline Recovery

## Title
Admin Forgot-Password via SuperAdmin Challenge-Response (Offline)

## Context
Admin loses access (forgot password). Existing self-service recovery (ADR-052) requires
the Admin to have previously set up a personal recovery keypair. When that is not in place,
the only path is SA-authorized recovery. The SA may be remote (cannot visit the campus)
so the mechanism must work over a phone call or SMS — no internet required between
SA's machine and the client system.

## Decision
Challenge-response protocol using SA's existing RSA keypair (ADR-053):
1. Admin opens /recovery → selects "SuperAdmin Recovery" tab → enters username.
2. Backend generates challenge, stores it with the username.
3. UI displays a short RECOVERY TOKEN: base32(sha256(challenge).slice(0,5)) — 8 chars.
4. Also displays full challenge hex for SA CLI input.
5. SA runs: license-cli sa-recovery-sign --challenge <hex> --private-key sa.pem
   → outputs base64 signature (the RESPONSE STRING).
6. Admin enters RESPONSE STRING into the UI.
7. Backend verifies RSA-PSS signature of the challenge using SA's stored public key.
8. On success: Admin sets new password; mustChangePassword flag set to true.

## Recovery Token Display
- Short token (8 chars, base32): for verbal phone confirmation that SA and Admin
  are working on the same challenge (prevents replay / confusion).
- Full challenge hex (64 chars): SA pastes into CLI to generate the signature.
- Response STRING: base64 RSA-PSS signature (~344 chars); transmitted via SMS/email/phone.

## Consequences
- SA recovery requires the SA to have their private key file available.
- No internet required between SA's machine and client system — fully offline.
- Recovery bypasses Admin's own password; mustChangePassword is forced after recovery.
- New backend routes: GET /auth/recovery/sa-challenge, POST /auth/recovery/sa-redeem.
- New CLI command: license-cli sa-recovery-sign.
- Frontend: new tab on existing /recovery page.

